# SPA fallback: serve index.html for client-side routes so that direct hits
# and search-engine landings on deep links (e.g. /json-formatter) resolve
# instead of 404ing. Honored by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.
#
# Other hosts need their own equivalent:
#   - Vercel:  add a rewrite { "source": "/(.*)", "destination": "/index.html" }
#   - Apache:  FallbackResource /index.html  (or a mod_rewrite rule)
#   - Nginx:   try_files $uri /index.html;
#   - GitHub Pages: copy index.html to 404.html
/*    /index.html   200
